/ One save button for both layouts, as the form-dirty controller knows one.
  Disabled from the start, as the form-dirty controller sets it on connect.
  Else it shows enabled until the controller connects.

  The save button comes first in the form, because Enter in a field submits
  with the first submit button. The delete button moves to the left edge with
  order-first.
.flex.items-center.justify-end.gap-3.mt-8.lg:mt-6
  button class=BUTTON_CLASS type="submit" disabled=true data-form-dirty-target="submit"
    = icon 'check', class: 'max-lg:hidden'
    = label
  - if delete_path
    = render Button::Component.new icon: removal[:icon],
                                   type: :submit,
                                   style: :secondary,
                                   options: { \
                                     **delete_options,
                                     title: removal[:label],
                                     data: { turbo_confirm: removal[:confirm], controller: 'tooltip' },
                                     class: 'order-first mr-auto max-lg:hidden text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 hover:text-orange-500 dark:hover:text-orange-500',
                                   }
- if delete_path
  .mt-3.lg:hidden
    = button_tag removal[:label],
                 type: :submit,
                 **delete_options,
                 data: { turbo_confirm: removal[:confirm] },
                 class: 'w-full rounded-full py-3.5 text-headline font-semibold click-animation transition-colors bg-red-500/10 text-signal-negative active:bg-red-500/20 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-red-500 focus:ring-offset-2 dark:focus:ring-offset-slate-900'
